# Nx workspace guidance

AGENTS.md contains the main Nx guidelines (use Nx for tasks, prefix with pnpm, use Nx MCP). This rule adds patterns for exploration and scaffolding.

## Exploration

- List projects: `pnpm nx show projects` (add `--json` for machine-readable).
- Project config: `pnpm nx show project <name> --json` (do not read project.json directly for full config; use this or Nx MCP).
- Targets: `pnpm nx show project <name> --json | jq '.targets | keys'`.
- Affected: `pnpm nx show projects --affected --json`; see docs for `nx affected` and base/head.

## Running tasks

- Single: `pnpm nx run <project>:<target>`.
- Many: `pnpm nx run-many -t <target> [-p project1,project2] [--exclude=...]`.
- Affected: `pnpm nx affected -t <target> [--base=main]`.

Use `--skipNxCache`, `--verbose`, `--nxBail` when needed. Prefer `nx run` / `nx run-many` / `nx affected` over running the underlying tool directly.

## Scaffolding

- For new apps/libs or project structure: run `pnpm nx g <generator> --help` then `pnpm nx g <generator> ... --no-interactive`.
- Prefer local workspace generators over plugin generators when both exist.
- Run with `--dry-run` first to verify file placement.
- List plugins: `pnpm nx list`. Add plugin: `pnpm nx add <plugin>`.

## CI

The repo uses `nx run-many -t lint build typecheck` in CI. Use `nx affected` in workflows when you want to run only for changed projects.
